ASSUMPTION CHALLENGE
--------------------
Alternate vertex sets considered: cauldrons/colors, active-state signatures, first-boil witnesses, removal order types, fixed arities, subset-sum obligations, residue classes, and proof routes.
Preserved predicate: survival of the selected additive boil relation over the current prefix.
Destroyed information: canonical active-state quotients forget cauldron labels; first-boil Schur quotients forget removal timing; finite-sums quotients forget which subset size caused failure unless witnesses are retained.
Challenged assumption: the literal game is not automatically classical Schur, because each natural is placed once and repeated summands require an extra rule.

